e SDK is globbing for .fsl files.\\n\\nActually, I just realized something. The F# compiler might be reading the .fsl file because it's being included as a source file by the F# targets. The Microsoft.FSharp.Targets might have a glob that includes .fsl files.\\n\\nLet me try a different approach: rename the .fsl file to something else, or move it to a different location.\\n\\nActually, the simplest fix might be to just clean the build and try again. The issue might be that the generated files are stale.\\n\", \"security_risk\": \"LOW\", \"summary\": \"Analyze why Lexer.fsl is being compiled despite not being in Compile list\"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-b01f2be1-1e17-4a3f-aa65-f3170ed3c66c", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Analyze why Lexer.fsl is being compiled despite not being in Compile list", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
